        "original_id": "20763313-36c1-5cac-a801-8b2b3c569eb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tionne Watkins, Park So-yeon, Lisa Lopes, Anita McLoud, Edmund \"Eddie Hustle\" Clement, Kandi Burruss, Babyface, Daryl Simmons\n- Organizations: TLC, T-ara\n- Products: \"Girl Talk\", \"Hands Up\", \"3D\"\n- Places: Des Moines, Iowa\n\nFacts:\n- Tionne Watkins was born in Des Moines, Iowa.\n- Tionne Watkins rose to fame in the early 1990s as a member of the girl group TLC.\n- Park So-yeon is best known as the former main vocalist and member of the South Korean girl group T-ara.\n- Lisa Lopes, Tionne Watkins, Anita McLoud, Edmund \"Eddie Hustle\" Clement, and Kandi Burruss wrote \"Girl Talk\" for TLC's fourth studio album \"3D\" in 2002.\n- Babyface and Daryl Simmons wrote and produced \"Hands Up\" for TLC's fourth studio album \"3D\" in 2002.\n- \"Hands Up\" was released in the United States in November 2002 as the second single from \"3D\" after \"Girl Talk\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
